# TinyMCE API Key Configuration
#
# OPTION 1: Use TinyMCE Cloud (Recommended - No console warnings)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Sign up for a FREE TinyMCE account at: https://www.tiny.cloud/auth/signup/
# 2. Get your API key from the dashboard
# 3. Copy this file to .env.local and add your API key below:
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TINYMCE_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
#
# Free tier includes 1,000 editor loads per month (sufficient for most projects)
#
# OPTION 2: Self-Hosted Mode (Current Default)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave the variable commented out or set to "no-api-key"
# This uses the local TinyMCE files in public/tinymce/
# You'll see a console warning but the editor will work fine.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TINYMCE_API_KEY=no-api-key

# To use this file:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.local.example .env.local
# 2. Add your TinyMCE API key in .env.local
# 3. Restart your development server: npm run dev
